Description: Build no effect preview for a removed effect row
 In 2D, a failed effect preview removes its row from the delegate's own
 onFailed handler. The removed row's delegate lives on until its deferred
 deletion, with index -1 and model.filters undefined. When the drawer opens
 again before that deletion, its description binding builds
 "... ! undefined name=last" and gst_parse_launch() refuses it with
 'no element "undefined"'. A delegate without its row now builds no
 pipeline and removes nothing. The test loads the real Config.qml with
 stand-ins for the types Kamoso registers in C++ and fails without the change.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-24

